## Context

The 0205 external-reviewer panel trial review (2026-10-02) found: empty
defect anchors make the audition payoff structurally zero; agent-authored
scorecards drift out of the parser; the seat-runner assumption blocks
runtime portability; decorrelation was never measured. The approved
redesign replaces seat execution with attribution capture. Spec:
docs/2026-10-02-reviewer-attribution-design.md — the single source of
truth for the record contract, skill split, statistics policy and
teardown.

TRACKING TICKET — stays open until all children merge, the teardown lands
and tickets/0205 is closed with its integration-review note.

## Children

- tickets/1005 — attribution record template + roar step-6 capture
  (blocked-by 0909: the memory v8 rollout defines the journal the records
  live in — author sequencing decision, coaching revamp comes AFTER the
  memory revamp; 1008 stays independent, it seeds the frozen board)
- tickets/1006 — post-merge defect backfill hook in roar step-3 sweep
  (blocked-by 1005)
- tickets/1007 — read surfaces: scores, correlation, marginal coverage;
  migrates enumerate-merges.py (blocked-by 1005)
- tickets/1008 — ground-truth seeding, absorbs tickets/0356
- tickets/1009 — teardown: reviewers write path, celebration telemetry,
  ticket dispositions (blocked-by 1005 — capture lands before teardown)

## Ordering

1008 is independent and can run at any time — it seeds the frozen
benchmark board, not memory. Capture (1005) waits for the memory v8
rollout (0909, author decision 2026-10-02), then 1006/1007 in any
order; teardown (1009) last: a teardown-first sequencing creates a
recording gap.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] 1005-1008 merged; attribution records capture writer/reviewer/
      findings/defects facts on every reviewed merge
- [ ] 1009 landed: reviewers skill thinned to descriptor+replay,
      celebration telemetry deleted, 0980 closed WONTDO, closed trial
      tickets annotated
- [ ] 0205 closed with integration-review note cross-referencing this
      tracker and the spec

## Raid annotation (2026-10-03, imagine pass)
PREMISE: The tracker's remaining scope is exactly the integration review after its children merge, plus box-ticking. Box-by-box at a6ff92d5: (1) PARTIAL — 1008 closed (PR #1121: board seeded, 23 entries / 17 defect-bearing / 6 justified-empty, test-anchored) and 0205 closed, but 1005/1006/1007 unmerged and zero attribution records exist in the tree; the "records capture facts on every reviewed merge" half is a continuous property that starts accruing only after 1005 lands. (2) FALSE — 1009 open; the celebration machinery and the full seat-runner reviewers skill are intact. (3) DONE (verification only, per log 2026-10-03T08:22Z) — 0205's close reason cross-references this tracker and the spec and delegates residual work to 1009 actions 3–4.
REIMAGINE: One end-to-end verification pass with named observable evidence. (a) Capture: ≥1 live record from a real reviewed merge after 1005 landed, parsing via the fixed-line reader (writer + verbatim model id + effort; one reviewer line per reviewer each with `status:`; repo-relative path:line anchors + adopted flags). (b) Backfill: the step-3 hook present; one real or simulated post-merge fix appended a defect-confirmed line, append-only, nothing else mutated. (c) Read surfaces: the `scripts/` query renders scores with Beta-Binomial 90% CrIs, the four-cell concordance, and marginal coverage from real records; malformed lines WARN on stderr; `enumerate-merges.py` lives in `scripts/`, not `skills/roar/`. (d) Teardown: reviewers = descriptor + replay pointer (no `panel.yml`, no scorecard/scores/audition machinery); grep-clean for `log-celebration` / `roar-last-sha` / `CLAUDE_TELEMETRY_DIR`; gaze panel section thinned with fail-open kept; 0980 closed WONTDO; 0356 close verified; annotation lines on all seven trial tickets. (e) The "every reviewed merge" claim is an enumeration, not a sample: enumerate merged PRs since 1005's merge commit and show each reviewed PR's record naming its reviewers; a gap is a §4.8 defect to report. (f) No dangling references: surviving mentions of removed machinery must be historical (closed-ticket logs, `docs/research/`), not operational; and the two inherited cross-ticket promises honored — 0205's note points at 1009 actions 3–4 (now executed), and 0937's closed box 3 is observable as `status: failed|skipped` lines in real records + the 1007 run-failure rate. (g) Tests green on the post-teardown reduced suite.
ANTIPATTERNS: No re-doing child work (if a child deliverable is defective, REROLL against that child's scope — do not silently patch under the tracker). No closing before 1009 lands (strands the §10 dispositions). No rubber-stamp integration note — tick boxes from the tree, never from ticket logs (the 0205 cautionary tale: its log claimed criteria satisfied while boxes stayed unticked). No touching 0870/0936/0902/0990 (internal panel, §10 "untouched" — confirm unchanged, do not absorb panel-integrity fixes into the teardown). No resurrecting trial verdicts or deleting scorecards. No backfilling reviewer names from memory (§4.8).
EXIT-CRITERIA: Box 1 — all four children in `tickets/closed/`; ≥1 live real-merge record parsing valid; a clean post-1005 enumeration with no capture gap (re-checked at close time). Box 2 — (d) above, in full. Box 3 — the note exists (it does) AND the work it delegates (1009 actions 3–4) is actually executed; confirm the workflow.md gradient survives with no seat reference creeping back in (the rule at `rules/workflow.md:107-108` is already seat-mechanism-free — action 4 is gradient completion, not a structural change). Verdict: keep-as-is (the annotation fills the one gap: the tracker never specifies what the integration review checks — that is (a)–(g) here).

